# The reduction to `ℂ`: `DivLoc` from the `∗`-regular closure over `ℂ`

The `∗`-regular closure of the image of `K[H]` in `U(G)` is generated by that image **together
with the stars of its elements**, and the epicity of the structure map `K[↥H] →+* V_K` — which the
construction `Work.ORHughesFree.Section6.thm61Step_nonempty` needs, and which is the reason the
JZLA20 engine is applied at the `∗`-regular closure rather than at `U(G)` — fails for a general
coefficient field `K`: the stars of the *scalars* `algebraMap K E.U k` need not be ring expressions
in the image.  See the counterexample in the docstring of
`Submission/Work/ORDivLoc/Closure/isEpic_starClosureCod.lean` (trivial group, `K = ℚ(α)`, `α` a
non-real cube root of `2`).

Over `ℂ` there is no such problem: `star (algebraMap ℂ E.U c) = algebraMap ℂ E.U (conj c)` by the
envelope's `ι_star` and `ι_algebraMap`, and `star (genU E h) = genU E h⁻¹`, so the structure map
`ℂ[↥H] →+* U(G)` is a `∗`-homomorphism.  Hence:

* `Work.ORDivLoc.isEpic_starClosureCod_complex` — the structure map into the `∗`-regular closure
  over `ℂ` is epic (via `Closure.isEpic_codRestrict_starRegularClosure_of_star_mem`);

and the route to `DivLoc` for an arbitrary `φK : K →+* ℂ` is

`V_K ⊆ V_ℂ`, `D_{K[H]}(U(G)) ⊆ V_K`, `V_ℂ` division closed in `U(G)`,

so that if `V_ℂ` is a division ring then every nonzero element of `D_{K[H]}(U(G))` has its inverse
in `V_ℂ ⊆ U(G)`, hence, by division closedness of `D_{K[H]}(U(G))`, in `D_{K[H]}(U(G))` itself.

This is R4 of `OR_REMAINING_LEAD.md` §3.1 in the form "reduce to `ℂ` and the `∗`-regular closure".
-/
import Submission.Work.ORDivLoc.N6
import Submission.Work.ORDivLoc.Rank.exists_faithful_sylvesterRank_starClosure

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false
set_option maxHeartbeats 1000000

universe u v

namespace Work.ORDivLoc

open Work.ORHughesFree

/-! ## The general bridge: a division-closed subring containing `D H` -/

/-- **The bridge in its most general form.**  Let `W ⊆ U(G)` be division closed and contain the
division closure `D_{K[H]}(U(G))`.  If every nonzero element of `W` is a unit of `W`, then every
nonzero element of `D_{K[H]}(U(G))` is a unit of `D_{K[H]}(U(G))`: the inverse of `x ∈ D H` lies in
`W ⊆ U(G)`, and `D H` is division closed in `U(G)`.

Both routes of the bridge (`W = V_K`, the `∗`-regular closure over `K`, and `W = V_ℂ`, the
`∗`-regular closure over `ℂ`) are instances of this statement. -/
theorem divOn_of_divisionClosed_le {G : Type v} [Group G] {K : Type u} [Field K]
    (E : Work.ORVonNeumann.StarRegularEnvelope G) (φK : K →+* ℂ) [Algebra K E.U]
    (H : Subgroup G) (W : Subring E.U) (hW : IsDivisionClosed W)
    (hDW : Work.ORBridgeLinnell.D E φK H ≤ W)
    (hdiv : ∀ x : ↥W, x ≠ 0 → IsUnit x) : DivOn E φK H := by
  intro x hx0
  have hxW : (x : E.U) ∈ W := hDW x.2
  have hxW0 : (⟨(x : E.U), hxW⟩ : ↥W) ≠ 0 := by
    intro h
    refine hx0 (Subtype.ext ?_)
    have h' := congrArg (fun z : ↥W => (z : E.U)) h
    simpa using h'
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := hdiv (⟨(x : E.U), hxW⟩ : ↥W) hxW0
  let w : ↥W := ((u⁻¹ : (↥W)ˣ) : ↥W)
  have hxw : (x : E.U) * (w : E.U) = 1 := by
    have h2 : (⟨(x : E.U), hxW⟩ : ↥W) * w = 1 := by rw [← hu]; exact Units.mul_inv u
    exact congrArg (fun z : ↥W => (z : E.U)) h2
  have hwmem : (w : E.U) ∈ Work.ORBridgeLinnell.D E φK H :=
    Work.ORBridgeLinnell.isDivisionClosed_D E φK H (x : E.U) x.2 (w : E.U) hxw
  have hwx : (w : E.U) * (x : E.U) = 1 := by
    have h2 : w * (⟨(x : E.U), hxW⟩ : ↥W) = 1 := by rw [← hu]; exact Units.inv_mul u
    exact congrArg (fun z : ↥W => (z : E.U)) h2
  exact isUnit_iff_exists.mpr ⟨⟨(w : E.U), hwmem⟩, Subtype.ext hxw, Subtype.ext hwx⟩

/-! ## The `∗`-regular closure over `ℂ` contains the one over `K` -/

/-- **The image of `K[H]` in `U(G)` is contained in the image of `ℂ[H]`**, for the canonical
`K`-algebra structure `Work.ORBridgeLinnell.kAlgebra E φK`: `k • genU h = (φK k) • genU h`. -/
theorem range_toUK_subset_range_toUK_complex {G : Type v} [Group G] {K : Type u} [Field K]
    (E : Work.ORVonNeumann.StarRegularEnvelope G) (φK : K →+* ℂ) [Algebra K E.U] (H : Subgroup G)
    (hφK : ∀ k : K, algebraMap K E.U k = algebraMap ℂ E.U (φK k)) :
    Set.range (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.toUK E φK H) ⊆
      Set.range (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.toUK E (RingHom.id ℂ) H) := by
  intro y hy
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hy
  induction x using MonoidAlgebra.induction_on with
  | of h =>
      exact ⟨MonoidAlgebra.of ℂ ↥H h,
        by rw [Work.ORBridgeLinnell.toUK_of, Work.ORBridgeLinnell.toUK_of]⟩
  | add x y hx hy =>
      obtain ⟨x', hx'⟩ := hx
      obtain ⟨y', hy'⟩ := hy
      exact ⟨x' + y', by rw [map_add, map_add, hx', hy']⟩
  | smul r x hx =>
      obtain ⟨x', hx'⟩ := hx
      refine ⟨φK r • x', ?_⟩
      rw [map_smul, map_smul, hx', Algebra.smul_def, Algebra.smul_def, hφK r]

/-- **`V_K ⊆ V_ℂ`**: the `∗`-regular closure of the image of `K[H]` in `U(G)` is contained in the
`∗`-regular closure of the image of `ℂ[H]`. -/
theorem starClosure_le_complex {G : Type v} [Group G] {K : Type u} [Field K]
    (E : Work.ORVonNeumann.StarRegularEnvelope G) (φK : K →+* ℂ) [Algebra K E.U] (H : Subgroup G)
    (hφK : ∀ k : K, algebraMap K E.U k = algebraMap ℂ E.U (φK k)) :
    (starClosureOfSubgroup E φK H).toSubring ≤
      (starClosureOfSubgroup E (RingHom.id ℂ) H).toSubring :=
  fun _ hx => StarRegular.starRegularClosure_mono
    (StarRegular.starSubringClosure_mono (range_toUK_subset_range_toUK_complex E φK H hφK)) hx

/-! ## R4: the division ring at the `∗`-regular closure over `ℂ` implies `DivLoc` -/

/-- **R4: `DivLoc` from the `∗`-regular closure over `ℂ`.**

If the `∗`-regular closure of the image of `ℂ[H]` in `U(G)` is a division ring, then the division
closure of `K[H]` in `U(G)` is a division ring, for *any* coefficient field `K` with an embedding
`φK : K →+* ℂ` compatible with the `K`-algebra structure of `U(G)`. -/
theorem divOn_of_complexClosureDivOn {G : Type v} [Group G] {K : Type u} [Field K]
    (E : Work.ORVonNeumann.StarRegularEnvelope G) (φK : K →+* ℂ) [Algebra K E.U] (H : Subgroup G)
    (hφK : ∀ k : K, algebraMap K E.U k = algebraMap ℂ E.U (φK k))
    (h : IsDivisionRing ↥(starClosureOfSubgroup E (RingHom.id ℂ) H)) : DivOn E φK H :=
  divOn_of_divisionClosed_le E φK H _ (isDivisionClosed_starClosureOfSubgroup E (RingHom.id ℂ) H)
    ((D_le_starClosureOfSubgroup E φK H).trans (starClosure_le_complex E φK H hφK))
    (fun x hx => h.2 x hx)

/-! ## Node N6's raw input at `ℂ`, and the deliverable at `Type` -/

/-- **Node N6's raw input over `ℂ`.**  The induction environment `Thm61Step` for the pair
`(↥H, V_ℂ)` and the structure map `ℂ[H] →+* V_ℂ`, where `V_ℂ` is the `∗`-regular closure of the
image of `ℂ[H]` in `U(G) = countableEnvelope G`, for every locally indicable `H ≤ G` and every
finitely generated non-trivial `H₀ ≤ ↥H`.

This is the conclusion of `Work.ORHughesFree.Section6.thm61Step_nonempty` over `ℂ`; its inputs are
positive definiteness of `V_ℂ`, a faithful Sylvester rank function on `V_ℂ`, the epicity
(`Work.ORDivLoc.isEpic_starClosureCod_complex`) and the `∗`-compatibility of the structure map, and
[JZLA20, Proposition 3.11] (`Work.ORDivLoc.Prop311OnComplex`). -/
def HstepOnComplex (G : Type) [Group G] [Countable G] : Prop :=
  ∀ H : Subgroup G, Work.ORLocInd.Group.LocallyIndicable H →
    ∀ H₀ : Subgroup ↥H, H₀.FG → H₀ ≠ ⊥ →
      Nonempty (Thm61Step ℂ ↥H
        (↥(starClosureOfSubgroup (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) (RingHom.id ℂ) H))
        (starClosureCod (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) (RingHom.id ℂ) H) H₀)

/-- `ClDivLoc` over `ℂ` for the canonical envelope: node N6's output at `ℂ`. -/
theorem clDivLoc_complex {G : Type} [Group G] [Countable G] (h : HstepOnComplex G) :
    ClDivLoc ℂ G (RingHom.id ℂ) := by
  intro H hLI
  exact clDivOn_of_hstep (RingHom.id ℂ) (h H hLI)

/-- **The deliverable at `Type`.**  From node N6's raw input over `ℂ` (`HstepOnComplex`) and the
epicity of the structure map into the `∗`-regular closure over `ℂ`
(`Work.ORDivLoc.isEpic_starClosureCod_complex`), `DivLoc K G φK` holds for **every** coefficient
field `K : Type` with an embedding `φK : K →+* ℂ`. -/
theorem divLoc_of_hstepComplex_of_epic {G : Type} [Group G] [Countable G] (h : HstepOnComplex G)
    (hEpic : ∀ H : Subgroup G, Work.ORLocInd.Group.LocallyIndicable H →
      IsEpic (starClosureCod (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) (RingHom.id ℂ) H))
    {K : Type} [Field K] (φK : K →+* ℂ) : DivLoc K G φK := by
  letI := Work.ORBridgeLinnell.kAlgebra (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) φK
  intro H hLI
  have hcl : ClDivOn (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) (RingHom.id ℂ) H :=
    clDivOn_of_hstep (RingHom.id ℂ) (h H hLI)
  have hV : IsDivisionRing
      ↥(starClosureOfSubgroup (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) (RingHom.id ℂ) H) :=
    starClosureDivOn_of_clDivOn (RingHom.id ℂ) (hEpic H hLI) hcl
  exact divOn_of_complexClosureDivOn _ φK H (fun k => rfl) hV

end Work.ORDivLoc
